      </li>
      <li>The number of nodes in the cluster</li>
      <li>The health of the cluster nodes</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="cluster-update-phases_openshift-update-duration" class="group scroll-mt-20">Cluster update phases<a href="#cluster-update-phases_openshift-update-duration" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">OpenShift Container Platform updates are done in multiple phases.</p>
      <p>The cluster update happens in the following two phases:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Cluster Version Operator (CVO) target update payload deployment</li>
      <li>Machine Config Operator (MCO) node updates</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 id="cluster-version-operator_openshift-update-duration" class="group scroll-mt-20">Cluster Version Operator target update payload deployment<a href="#cluster-version-operator_openshift-update-duration" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p class="_abstract">In the first phase of the update, the Cluster Version Operator (CVO) retrieves the target update release image and applies to the cluster.</p>
      <p>All components which run as pods are updated during this phase, whereas the host components are updated by the Machine Config Operator (MCO). This process might take 60 to 120 minutes.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
